# Three Blind Mice. Chapter II says "target token you control": Bot2's Goblin tokens and Bot1's nontoken Memnite are not legal targets, so
# the Mouse is the only one and chapter II targets it without asking (a Goblin or the Memnite as a legal target would make it
# ask). Turn 4 Bot2 makes two Goblin tokens; on turn 5 the Mouse is copied, and Bot1 has no Goblin.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Memnite
Three Blind Mice
Plains x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Dragon Fodder
Mountain x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Three Blind Mice.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain#1.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain#2.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Dragon Fodder.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mouse Token#2.Power = 1
? Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 4
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 7

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 4
